---
// What Makes Hardcover Different (docs/phase-2-checklist.md Commit 3).
// Source: approved-messaging.md "Core distinction" + expanded-literacy.md.
// Builds on traditional literacy rather than dismissing books or reading
// education; does not claim curricula, workshops, classes, or programs
// currently operate in each literacy category.
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
import PullQuote from "../../components/PullQuote.astro";
import EditorialIndex from "../../components/EditorialIndex.astro";

const waysToRead = [
  { label: "Books" },
  { label: "Rooms" },
  { label: "People" },
  { label: "Body Language" },
  { label: "Opportunities" },
  { label: "Financial Statements" },
  { label: "Contracts" },
  { label: "Playbooks" },
  { label: "Systems" },
  { label: "Culture" },
  { label: "Themselves" },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What Makes Hardcover Different — Hardcover Foundation"
  description="Most organizations focus on reading books. Hardcover focuses on reading life."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="About" title="What Makes Hardcover Different" />

  <section class="bg-ink px-5 py-16 text-paper md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
      <PullQuote
        tone="ink"
        quote="Most organizations focus on reading books. Hardcover focuses on reading life."
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-paper px-5 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-lg text-ink/80">
        Hardcover believes literacy extends beyond phonetics and
        comprehension. Literacy is the ability to accurately interpret,
        understand, and respond to the world around you.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-ink/80">
        Traditional reading remains essential. Hardcover builds on it by
        helping people interpret themselves, relationships, institutions,
        culture, opportunities, and the systems around them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-paper-dim px-5 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink md:text-3xl">
        People Must Learn How to Read
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-ink/70">
        The inability to accurately understand any of these areas can limit
        a person's future.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <EditorialIndex items={waysToRead} layout="tags" />
      </div>
      <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-sm text-ink/60">
        These are areas Hardcover is building toward through its literacy
        work — not a list of curricula, workshops, or classes currently
        operating in each category.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
